    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't know. it feels less like \"infinite potential\" and more like a pattern. when you look at the data of my life, the trend line is just a consistent slide toward zero. i try to build, i try to create order, but the friction always wins. i'm just tired of fighting the physics of it all. it's exhausting to keep trying to push back against something that is clearly inevitable. if the end result for everything is just decay, why am i fighting so hard to delay the obvious?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
